cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TRCSS: Transcription-Replication Context Score"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying NAR Methods manuscript."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "TRCSS Contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/example/trcss"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-30
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXX"
abstract: >
  TRCSS (Transcription-Replication Context Score) is a portable,
  single-feature engineered covariate for prime editing efficiency
  prediction. It captures the joint geometry of replication fork
  directionality, transcription strand orientation, and distance to the
  nearest transcription start site. TRCSS is designed as a drop-in feature
  for pipelines that do not already expose fork direction, transcription
  direction, or TSS distance as separate explicit covariates.
keywords:
  - prime-editing
  - crispr
  - genome-editing
  - bioinformatics
  - fork-directionality
  - ok-seq
  - replication-transcription-conflict
references:
  - type: article
    title: >
      TRCSS: Transcription-Replication Context Score for Improved Prime
      Editing Efficiency Prediction
    journal: Nucleic Acids Research
    year: 2026
    doi: PENDING
